// Relativization / partition-safety, `count >= 2`, with THREE keys interleaved.
//
// Extends 1157 (2-key count) to two DISTINCT foreign principals. The count
// encoding tallies mine-positions in a range; this exercises it when bob AND
// carol both have Logins interspersed among alice's — the case that would
// expose a range-count that miscounts (over- or under-counts) when multiple
// distinct foreign keys populate the scan range.
//
// The count body does not correlate on user (`Login{ input.user: _ }`), so the
// pin is the only thing confining the count. Two pairs, each with/without the
// foreign events:
//
//   DENY pair — alice has ONE own Login; bob and carol have logins too. A
//   correct key-local count = 1 (< 2) -> DENY. A global (or leak) count would
//   tally alice+bob+carol -> >= 2 -> permit.
//     trace_1: alice Login, BOB Login, CAROL Login, alice Read.
//     trace_2: alice Login,                         alice Read.
//
//   PERMIT pair — alice has TWO own Logins; bob and carol interleaved are inert.
//     trace_3: alice Login, BOB Login, alice Login, CAROL Login, alice Read.
//     trace_4: alice Login,            alice Login,              alice Read.
//   Correct key-local count = 2 (>= 2) -> PERMIT in both; two distinct foreign
//   keys neither add to nor block alice's tally.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). (
        (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
            formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: _ } && tp(t))
        )) == n && n >= 2
    )
};
